camchrome: a Windows persona's fonts answer by every name, and its text lays out like DirectWrite.

Clearcote audit, Windows persona on a Linux host (with 040's clone fonts installed):

- "a Windows CJK font answers to its localized family name": 11 of the 15 English/localized pairs
  DirectWrite answers to were missing (新宋体, 微軟正黑體, 游ゴシック, 맑은 고딕, ...). They are on the
  Windows font list now and render through their English twin's clone, so both names measure
  identically.
- "core Windows fonts that measure as installed also load by name": local() asked the host's
  unique-name table only. A miss now retries with the persona's clone for names on the persona
  OS's font list (Calibri -> Carlito); other names still miss.
- "text layout uses the font scaler of the operating system claimed": under a Windows or macOS
  persona, text is unhinted with linear, subpixel-positioned advances, as DirectWrite and CoreText
  lay it out; stepping the size by 0.01 px changes the width on nearly every step. Linux and
  Android personas keep FreeType's own behaviour.

